Add({
	id = "mulgore",
	title = "Mulgore",
	aliases = { "the plains of Mulgore" },
	faction = "Horde",
	continent = "Kalimdor",
	maps = { 1412, 7 },
	zone = "Mulgore",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "zone" },
		{ type = "map" },
	},
	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Mulgore is the homeland of the {link:tauren}tauren{/link}, a wide country of golden grass and gentle hills walled in by mountains on every side. Kodo herds graze its plains, and clear wells and lakes water the land. Over it all stand the great mesas of {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link}, the tauren capital, where the High Chieftain {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} keeps his lodge. To the tauren this is the gift of the {red:earth-mother}Earth Mother{/red}, a peaceful land after centuries of wandering. Yet {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link}, gnolls, harpies and goblins press in from every edge, and the young of the tribes must prove themselves against them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[For countless generations the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} were nomads who followed the herds across the plains of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. The {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} hunted them without mercy, drove them from their old lands and scattered their tribes. {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link} of the Bloodhoof set himself to gather his people and lead them to a land where they could live in safety.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} were driven out, but Mulgore is not at rest. The {link:bristleback-quilboar}Bristleback quilboar{/link} war on the young {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of {link:red-cloud-mesa}Red Cloud Mesa{/link} and defile the burial ground of {link:red-rocks}Red Rocks{/link}. {link:palemane-gnolls}Palemane gnolls{/link} hunt the wildlife to ruin and answer every word of peace with blades. {link:windfury-harpies}Windfury harpies{/link} nest on the ridges. The goblins of the {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link} have poisoned the sacred wells and dug a mine into the eastern cliffs, and dwarves dig for old secrets in the west. In these days a band of Galak centaur has been seen again inside the borders, and a {link:longwalkers}Longwalker{/link} sent to watch the east did not come home. In the north-west, the shamans of the {link:earthen-ring}Earthen Ring{/link} have raised a camp where a strange people arrives from the sky: {link:skyborne}Skyborne{/link} elves of the {link:windshapers}Windshapers{/link}, come down from {link:skywall}Skywall{/link} to seek new allies.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:tauren}tauren{/link}.{/b} Hunters, shamans, druids and braves live in {link:camp-narache}Camp Narache{/link}, {link:bloodhoof-village}Bloodhoof Village{/link} and the city above. Chief {link:baine-bloodhoof}Baine Bloodhoof{/link}, son of {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link}, leads the village.
• {b}The {link:earthen-ring}Earthen Ring{/link}.{/b} Shamans of several peoples gather at {link:camp-gev-rek}Camp Gev'rek{/link} under {link:muln-earthfury}Muln Earthfury{/link}.
• {b}{link:bristleback-quilboar}Bristleback quilboar{/link}.{/b} They hold {link:brambleblade-ravine}Brambleblade Ravine{/link} and raid the mesa and the plains.
• {b}{link:palemane-gnolls}Palemane gnolls{/link}.{/b} They lair in {link:palemane-rock}Palemane Rock{/link} and in camps along the southern hills.
• {b}{link:windfury-harpies}Windfury harpies{/link}.{/b} They roost on the mountain edges of the south-east and on {link:windfury-ridge}Windfury Ridge{/link}.
• {b}The {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link}.{/b} Goblin miners, loggers and overseers who want the land emptied of its people.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Long March.{/b} Near the shores of the Great Sea, the young warchief {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} came upon {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link}'s people under {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} attack. The orcs escorted the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} caravans across {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link} to Mulgore, and in return Cairne showed Thrall the way to the Oracle of {link:stonetalon-mountains}Stonetalon{/link}.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} Cairne pledged his people to the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, and tauren warriors fought beside the orcs at the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}.
• {b}The Claiming of Mulgore.{/b} With the help of the Horde, the tauren broke the centaur's hold on the plains and made Mulgore a permanent home for all their tribes. On the mesas they raised {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Plains",
			text = [=[• A young {link:tauren}tauren{/link} earns a place in {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link} through the {link:rites-of-the-earthmother}Rites of the Earthmother{/link}, which lead from {link:camp-narache}Camp Narache{/link} to the lodge of the High Chieftain.
• In the south-eastern hills, above the mesa, stands a shrine to An'she and Mu'sha, the sun and the moon. The tauren honor the twins because their light gives life and guidance, though they are not of the world as the elements are.
• West of Stonebull Lake, a prairie wolf the hunters call Chakuyak stalks from one stand of trees to the next.]=],
		},
	},
})

